            "description": "[confidence=low, sources=static] [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The malware string 'CreateFile' was found in the binary. This string is characteristic of Indicator Removal on Host behavior. The presence of this specific string alone (no other Indicator Removal on Host-related string corroborates it) indicates the malware has capabilities associated with this technique, but with less certainty than a corroborated combination would. | [from D3D11InstallHelper.dll] The API functions CreateFileW, CreateFileA are imported by the binary. Each is individually associated with Indicator Removal on Host, but this specific combination doesn't form one of the corroborating patterns known to indicate Indicator Removal on Host with high confidence \u2014 treat this as suggestive rather than conclusive. | [from 66VOAk0O.exe] The malware string 'CreateFile' was found in the binary. This string is characteristic of Indicator Removal on Host behavior. The presence of this specific string alone (no other Indicator Removal on Host-related string corroborates it) indicates the malware has capabilities associated with this technique, but with less certainty than a corroborated combination would. | [from 66VOAk0O.exe] The API function 'CreateFileW' is imported by the binary. This API is commonly used to perform Indicator Removal on Host. Importing this function alone (no other Indicator Removal on Host-related import corroborates it) indicates the malware has the capability to execute this technique, but with less certainty than a corroborated combination would.",
